Files derived from FedMultimodal and modified for FedPCD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following files contain code from FedMultimodal and have been modified.
Each such file carries a prominent notice at the top of the file.

    constants/constants.py
    dataloader/dataload_manager.py
    model/common_fusions.py
    model/mm_models.py
    model/unimodal_models.py
    trainers/evaluation.py
    trainers/fed_avg_trainer.py
    trainers/fed_rs_trainer.py
    trainers/optimizer.py
    trainers/scaffold_trainer.py
    trainers/server_trainer.py
    features/data_partitioning/partition_manager.py
    features/data_partitioning/uci-har/data_partition.py
    features/feature_processing/feature_manager.py
    features/feature_processing/uci-har/extract_feature.py
    features/feature_processing/ku-har/extract_feature.py
    features/simulation_features/simulation_manager.py
    features/simulation_features/uci-har/simulation_feature.py
    experiment/uci-har/train.py
    experiment/ku-har/train.py

Summary of modifications to these files:

    - Removed the "fed_multimodal." package prefix and switched to
      repository-root imports so the code runs from a single checkout.
    - Added the FedPCD training path: global knowledge distillation (GKD:
      logit, feature, and cross-modal terms), cross-modal projection recovery
      (CPR), and Prototype-Cross Alignment (PCA).
    - Added client-level modality missingness: client-level mask loading,
      deterministic fixed client-to-modality assignments, and clean
      (complete-modality) dev/test evaluation.
    - Added the per-client missing-rate computation for the distillation
      schedule (Eq. 19): m_k = 0 for complete-modality clients and m_k = 1
      for single-modality clients.
    - Added the mHealth two-modality pipeline and the fixed Dirichlet client
      partitions for mHealth (beta=0.1) and KU-HAR (beta=0.3). The partitions
      are included as data because the original one-off generator is not part
      of this release.
    - Added the HAR experiment entry points used in the paper and the
      evaluation under incomplete test inputs.
    - Restricted the release to the three HAR datasets used in the paper;
      unused datasets and experiment scripts were removed.

